; lang.xon -- what this bundle is.
;
; xon: read with the ordinary reader and never evaluated, like every manifest
; in the x-lang world (pin.xon, engine.pin.xon). An unknown form is a loud
; error, never a silent skip.
;
; FORMAT (one form per line):
;   (lang "NAME")               the -l name
;   (dialect NAME)              he | xe | rn -- a requirement
;   (requires-release "TAG")    the x-lang this bundle was built against
;   (requires-lang "NAME" ["V"]) another lang this one is written on top
;                               of, optionally at an exact version
;   (entry "FILE")              loaded AFTER the dialect, not instead of it

(lang "r7rs")

; Xenon: Scheme's numerics are the tower. Not radon, because the two modules
; that wanted dlopen -- x/bytevector.x and scm/ports.scm -- are not loaded in
; this release.
(dialect xe)

; The x-lang release this bundle is built and tested against; CI compares it
; for equality.

(requires-release "v0.14.0")

; R7RS is R5RS plus about 700 lines, and this row is what says so. x.sh
; resolves it the way it resolves -l, arms the required lang's root before this
; bundle's own (import-path! prepends, so a shared name still resolves to ours),
; and refuses at startup naming what is missing and who asked.
;
; The version is compared for equality, never parsed -- the same rule as
; (requires-release ...) above -- so it names what this was built and tested
; against, not a minimum, and every x-r5rs release obsoletes the row.
; --allow-lang-skew is the way through while working on both at once.
;
; What the version compares against is derived: `make install` and
; tools/bundle.sh stamp a `version` file from git describe, so a checkout
; (which carries no stamp) does not satisfy the row -- only an install or an
; unpacked release tarball does.
;
; v0.2.0 is a floor this bundle cannot run below: the string ports are built on
; that release's polymorphic %strsrc/%strsink, which v0.1.0 lacks. Against
; v0.1.0 this bundle fails to load, not a spec.
(requires-lang "r5rs" "v0.2.3")

(entry "run.x")
